  "english": "Of [the Martyr] Astuatsatur. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"ok\"]: \"Who art exalted.\"\n8. Saturday. Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"DK\"]. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\n9. Sunday. Tone 1 [First Tone, \"ADz\"]. Fifth [Sunday]. Feast of the Barekendan [Pre-Lenten Eve] of the Fast of the Holy Cross. Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 1 [First Tone, \"a\"]: \"With the women.\"\n10. Monday. Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"AK\"]. Fast of the Holy Cross. [Hymn for the] Father: [Tone] 3: \"Glorified is Thy name.\"\n16. Sunday. Tone 6 [Second Plagal, \"GK\"]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. From here until the tenth Sunday, see the First Volume, maintaining the proper order of this place.\n23. Sunday. Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"DDz\"]. Second [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"ddz\"]: \"With an awesome voice.\"\n24. Monday. Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"DK\"]. Fast of the Cross of Varag. [Commemoration of] Mamas, etc. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 3 [Second Tone, \"b3\"]: \"Forbearing.\"\n26. Wednesday. Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"AK\"]. [Hymn for the] Father of penitence: Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"g3\"]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord God of our fathers,\" and \"Who wonderfully.\"\n30. Sunday. Tone 6 [Second Plagal, \"GK\"]. Third [Sunday]. Feast of the Cross of Varag. The period of non-fasting is seven weeks. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nOctober\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"GDz\"]. Fourth [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"g3\"]: \"The oil-bearing women,\" and \"Today the resurrection,\" and \"In the sign of the Cross.\"\n14. Sunday. Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"BK\"]. Fifth [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"bk\"]: \"Christ is risen,\" and \"In the morning.\"\n21. Sunday. Tone 3 [Second Tone, \"BDz\"]. Sixth [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 3 [Second Tone, \"b3\"]: \"In the tomb,\" and \"They came to the tomb,\" and \"The voice of good tidings.\"\n28. Sunday. Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"AK\"]. Seventh [Sunday]. Discovery of the Cross.\n30. Tuesday. Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"BK\"]. The Hyperichians, and Severian of Sebaste, etc. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"ak\"]: \"Who art exalted.\"\n31. Wednesday. Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"GDz\"]. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"gdz\"]: \"O God of our fathers, who in affliction.\" See the others in the First Volume unto the end, maintaining the proper order of this place.\n\nNovember\n\n3. Saturday. Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"DK\"]. All Saints, old and new, known and unknown.\n4. Sunday. Tone 1 [First Tone, \"ADz\"]. Eighth [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 1 [First Tone, \"adz\"]: \"Ineffable.\"\n23. Monday. Tone 1 [First Tone, \"ADz\"]. Anton [Anthony] the Hermit.\n24. Tuesday. Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"AK\"]. King Theodosius and the Children of Ephesus.\n26. Thursday. Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"BK\"]. Cyriacus and Julietta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"ddz\"]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord.\"\n28. Saturday. Tone 6 [Second Plagal, \"GK\"]. Athanasius and Cyril, and Gregory the Theologian.\n29. Sunday. Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"DDz\"]. Fifth [Sunday]. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"bk\"]: \"Unoriginate God.\" Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"ddz\"]: \"The women anticipating.\"\n30. Monday. Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"DK\"]. Vahan of Goghtn and Eugenia the Virgin, etc. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"dk\"]: \"To Thee, O God.\"\n31. Tuesday. Tone 1 [First Tone, \"ADz\"]. Tryphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the Hermits. Morning [Hymn]: Tone 1 [First Tone, \"a\"]: \"Who surpassed,\" with its canons.\n\n[August / Transfiguration Season]\n\n2. Thursday. Tone 3 [Second Tone, \"BDz\"]. Eugenius, Macarius, etc. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 8 [Plagal 4, \"dk\"]: \"Who the wondrous.\"\n4. Saturday. Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"GDz\"]. The Holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\n5. Sunday. Tone 6 [Second Plagal, \"GK\"]. Sixth [Sunday]. Barekendan [Pre-Lenten Eve] of the Fast of the Mother of God. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"g3\"]: \"We glorify.\" Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 6 [Second Plagal, \"gk\"]: \"By Thy divine tomb.\"\n6. Monday. Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"DDz\"]. Fast of the Mother of God. [Hymn for the] Father of penitence: Tone 3 [Second Tone, \"b3\"]: \"Who art awesome.\"\n12. Sunday. Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"GDz\"]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The period of non-fasting is three weeks.\n22. Wednesday. Tone 7 [Third Plagal, \"DDz\"]. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"bk\"]: \"The captive youths.\" See the middle period in the First Volume until the fourth Sunday.\n\nSeptember\n\n2. Sunday. Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"AK\"]. Fourth [Sunday]. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 5 [Third Tone, \"g3\"]: \"Glorified Son.\" Hambartsi [Hymn at Evening]: Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"ak\"]: \"The Lord risen from the tomb.\"\n3. Monday. Tone 3 [Second Tone, \"BDz\"]. Andrew the Commander and his army, etc.\n4. Tuesday. Tone 4 [Second Plagal, \"BK\"]. Adrian and his wife Anatolia, etc. [Hymn for the] Father: Tone 2 [First Plagal, \"ak\"]: \"Holy God Creator.\"\n6. Thursday. Tone 6 [Second Plagal, \"GK\"]. Abraham and Khoren, and Cosmas and Damian, and",
